BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:New Wave
DTSTART:20250924T020000Z
DTEND:20250924T035500Z
DTSTAMP:20250924T020000Z
UID:g07hNH9WOs
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 94 mins (1h34m)\n\nThe Popcorn List Mile-high hair. 
 Synthesized music. Underground parties. Elizabeth Ai’s lively first feat
 ure delves into the rebellious Vietnamese new wave blending nostalgia with
  a deeply personal re-examination of her community's music scene\, hidden 
 and unexamined past.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/the-popco
 rn-list/new-wave
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cinema Dissection: Point Blank
DTSTART:20250928T170000Z
DTEND:20250928T232000Z
DTSTAMP:20250928T170000Z
UID:ZS6Bc5uGXL
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 360 mins (6h00m)\n\nFilm Talks Combining a classic h
 ardboiled crime story with an expansive\, visual style highly influenced b
 y European New Wave filmmakers\, director John Boorman delivered what has 
 become a quintessential neo-noir. Lee Marvin stars as Walker\, a low-level
 \, hard-as-nails criminal whose partner just left him for dead and abscond
 ed with his cut of a $93\,000 heist and Walker’s wife. Walker tracks his
  partner to Los Angeles seeking his cut of the loot—and vengeance\, too
 —only to get entangled in the byzantine machinations of the Organization
 \, a new kind of criminal syndicate more concerned with stocks and bonds t
 han bullets\, babes\, or even cold\, hard cash. Join facilitator and SIFF 
 Programmer Dan Doody on a scene-by-scene breakdown of this seminal L.A. cr
 ime story. Ahead of this cinema dissection\, Point Blank screens September
  17 at SIFF Cinema Uptown as part of Greg Olson Productions L.A. Noir: Sha
 dows in Paradise film series.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/
 education/adult-film-education/film-talks/cinema-dissection-point-blank
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Balconettes
DTSTART:20251003T232000Z
DTEND:20251004T012500Z
DTSTAMP:20251003T232000Z
UID:4XDlmmBiHn
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 104 mins (1h44m)\n\nNoémie Merlant (Portrait of a L
 ady on Fire) co-writes\, directs\, and stars in this genre-bending feminis
 t comic thriller\, as a trio of Marseille roommates—a camgirl\, a writer
 \, and an actress—rage against toxic masculinity in the middle of a terr
 ible heat wave.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/the-balconettes
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Inter Alia
DTSTART:20251004T020000Z
DTEND:20251004T052000Z
DTSTAMP:20251004T020000Z
UID:5JKZRiRPfS
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 180 mins (3h00m)\n\nStage to Screen Oscar-nominated 
 Rosamund Pike (Gone Girl\, Saltburn) is Jessica in the much-anticipated ne
 xt play from the team behind Prima Facie. Jessica Parks is a smart Crown C
 ourt Judge at the top of her career. Behind the robe\, she is a karaoke fi
 end\, a loving wife and a supportive parent. When an event threatens to th
 row her life completely off balance\, can she hold her family upright?\n\n
 https://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/stage-to-screen/nt-live-inter-ali
 a
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
